# Single authority for the toolchain and registry pins used to check and
# publish this repository's packages. Both hosts read this file: the workflows
# source it into $GITHUB_ENV, and the Makefile includes it. Nothing else may
# restate these values -- scripts/verify-pins.sh asserts every literal copy
# that cannot read this file (a workflow `uses:` ref, the `hew-cabi` Cargo
# `rev`, the prose pin in docs/toolchain.md) against it.
#
# Sourced, never executed; each consumer uses a subset of the pins.
# See docs/toolchain.md for what each pin means and how to bump one.
#
#   HEW_REVISION       hew commit the packages are checked and published against
#   HEW_VERSION        version string that commit's binary must report
#   LLVM_VERSION       LLVM toolchain needed to build that commit
#   REGISTRY_API       registry endpoint scripts/publish-packages.sh publishes to
#   REGISTRY_AUDIENCE  OIDC audience for trusted publishing
# shellcheck disable=SC2034
HEW_REVISION=eb32407010b2932744fe420e69468f18240b3327
HEW_VERSION=0.6.0-rc3-dev.1012+eb3240701
LLVM_VERSION=22.1.5
REGISTRY_API=https://registry.hewpkg.com/api/v1
REGISTRY_AUDIENCE=https://registry.hewpkg.com
